USC: don't combine memory loads into a fetch across a store

BuildFetchInstructions groups loads from consecutive addresses in a block
into one fetch at the position of the earliest, however far apart they are,
so a load after a store moved before it and read the old memory: after
copying into local memory, then copying over part of it and copying it out
again, the copy out took the first element from the earlier fetch.  Only
combine two loads if no store which may write the later one's memory (or a
lock, release or synchronised load) is between them.  The alias check is
dgraph.c's, made public.

